{"absent":["AUSENTE: memory-mapped access method, barriers and ordering for these registers","AUSENTE: locking, concurrency and atomicity rules for send and overlay programming","AUSENTE: reset values, initialization order and firmware versus kernel ownership","AUSENTE: encodings for delivery mode, destination mode, socket count, key-width, GRU count and M_IO with N_IO","AUSENTE: side effects, completion and error reporting of the send trigger","AUSENTE: full field layout of the RH10 MMR overlay control beyond its gated base visible here"],"dossier":"D10","findings":[{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_IPI_INT_VECTOR_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_IPI_INT_VECTOR_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_IPI_INT_DELIVERY_MODE_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_IPI_INT_DELIVERY_MODE_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_IPI_INT_DESTMODE_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_IPI_INT_DESTMODE_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_IPI_INT_APIC_ID_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_IPI_INT_APIC_ID_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_IPI_INT_SEND_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_IPI_INT_SEND_MASK"],"text":"The IPI trigger register places an 8-bit vector at bit 0, a 3-bit delivery mode at bit 8, a 1-bit destination mode at bit 11, a 32-bit APIC identifier at bit 16, and a 1-bit send control at bit 63, with corresponding select masks covering the low byte, bits 8 to 10, bit 11, bits 16 to 47, and the top bit."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_ipi_int_u","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_ipi_int_u.uvh_ipi_int_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_ipi_int_u.uv5h_ipi_int_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_ipi_int_u.uv4h_ipi_int_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_ipi_int_u.uv3h_ipi_int_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_ipi_int_u.uv2h_ipi_int_s"],"text":"A 64-bit overlay pairs a raw value with common and UV2 through UV5 views that share one partition from low to high of vector then delivery mode then destination mode then a small reserved gap then APIC identifier then a larger reserved gap then send, where the payload selectors are readable and writable while send uses write-trigger semantics."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_ID","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_ID_FORCE1_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_ID_FORCE1_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_ID_MANUFACTURER_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_ID_MANUFACTURER_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_ID_PART_NUMBER_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_ID_PART_NUMBER_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_ID_REVISION_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_ID_REVISION_MASK"],"text":"Node identification is anchored at offset zero and its low word holds a single fixed bit at position 0, an 11-bit manufacturer code starting at bit 1, a 16-bit part number starting at bit 12, and a 4-bit revision starting at bit 28."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_id_u","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_id_u.uvh_node_id_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_id_u.uvxh_node_id_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_id_u.uvyh_node_id_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_id_u.uv5h_node_id_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_id_u.uv4h_node_id_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_id_u.uv3h_node_id_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_id_u.uv2h_node_id_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVXH_NODE_ID_NODE_ID_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_NODE_ID_NODE_ID_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV4H_NODE_ID_ROUTER_SELECT_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV3H_NODE_ID_ROUTER_SELECT_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_ID_NODE_ID_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_ID_NI_PORT_SHFT"],"text":"The node identifier overlay preserves the low identity block across all views while the upper half diverges by generation, with a generic view leaving it reserved, an XH view exposing a wider node number plus density and port telemetry, a YH and UV5 view exposing a narrower node number plus a wider port field, and UV3 and UV4 views adding a router selector alongside density and port fields."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_PRESENT_0","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_PRESENT_1","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_PRESENT_TABLE","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_PRESENT_TABLE_DEPTH","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_NODE_PRESENT_0_NODES_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_NODE_PRESENT_0_NODES_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_NODE_PRESENT_1_NODES_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_NODE_PRESENT_1_NODES_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVXH_NODE_PRESENT_TABLE_NODES_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVXH_NODE_PRESENT_TABLE_NODES_MASK"],"text":"Presence appears as full-width bitmaps starting at bit 0, with UV5 providing two single registers at offsets 0x1400 and 0x1408 and older generations providing a table at base 0x1400 whose depth is 4 on UV4 and 16 on UV2 and UV3, evaluating to zero when the revision does not match."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_present_0_u","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_present_0_u.uvh_node_present_0_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_present_1_u","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_present_1_u.uvh_node_present_1_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_present_table_u","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_present_table_u.uvh_node_present_table_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_present_table_u.uvxh_node_present_table_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_present_table_u.uv4h_node_present_table_s"],"text":"Each presence register overlays a raw 64-bit word with views that treat the entire width as a single writable nodes bitmap, with singleton variants for the newer family and table-entry variants for XH and UV2 through UV4."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_RH10_GAM_ADDR_MAP_CONFIG","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_ADDR_MAP_CONFIG_N_SKT_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_ADDR_MAP_CONFIG_N_SKT_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_ADDR_MAP_CONFIG_LS_ENABLE_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_ADDR_MAP_CONFIG_LS_ENABLE_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_ADDR_MAP_CONFIG_MK_TME_KEYID_BITS_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_ADDR_MAP_CONFIG_MK_TME_KEYID_BITS_MASK"],"text":"On UV5 the RH10 address-map control lives at 0x470000 and carries a 3-bit socket count at bit 6, a 1-bit local-storage enable at bit 12, and a 4-bit encryption key identifier width at bit 16, with undefined gaps around them and a large reserved high region."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_RH10_GAM_GRU_OVERLAY_CONFIG","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_GRU_OVERLAY_CONFIG_BASE_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_GRU_OVERLAY_CONFIG_BASE_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_GRU_OVERLAY_CONFIG_N_GRU_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_GRU_OVERLAY_CONFIG_N_GRU_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_GRU_OVERLAY_CONFIG_ENABLE_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_GRU_OVERLAY_CONFIG_ENABLE_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_RH10_GAM_GRU_OVERLAY_CONFIG_BASE_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_RH10_GAM_GRU_OVERLAY_CONFIG_BASE_SHFT"],"text":"On UV5 the GRU overlay control lives at 0x4700b0 and holds a 27-bit base starting at bit 25, a 3-bit GRU count starting at bit 52, and a 1-bit enable at the top bit, while generic helpers report the same base position and mask on UV5 and a zero mask with a negative shift otherwise."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_addr_map_config_u","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_addr_map_config_u.uvh_rh10_gam_addr_map_config_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_gru_overlay_config_u","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_gru_overlay_config_u.uvh_rh10_gam_gru_overlay_config_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_gru_overlay_config_u.uvyh_rh10_gam_gru_overlay_config_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_gru_overlay_config_u.uv5h_rh10_gam_gru_overlay_config_s"],"text":"Both RH10 controls overlay a raw word with common and family views that keep functional fields writable and preserve the same low-to-high order, namely undefined gaps around socket, enable and key-width settings for the address-map control and undefined low space then base then count then an undefined gap then enable for the GRU overlay."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_OVERLAY_CONFIG0","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_OVERLAY_CONFIG0_BASE_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_OVERLAY_CONFIG0_BASE_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_OVERLAY_CONFIG0_M_IO_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_OVERLAY_CONFIG0_M_IO_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_OVERLAY_CONFIG0_ENABLE_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_OVERLAY_CONFIG0_ENABLE_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_OVERLAY_CONFIG1","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_OVERLAY_CONFIG1_BASE_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_OVERLAY_CONFIG1_BASE_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_OVERLAY_CONFIG1_M_IO_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_OVERLAY_CONFIG1_M_IO_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_OVERLAY_CONFIG1_ENABLE_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_OVERLAY_CONFIG1_ENABLE_MASK"],"text":"On UV5 the two high MMIO overlay controls live at 0x473000 and 0x474000 and share one format of a 26-bit base at bit 26, a 6-bit M_IO selector at bit 52 with an adjacent 4-bit N_IO companion, and a 1-bit enable at the top bit, where base and M_IO are writable."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_mmioh_overlay_config0_u","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_mmioh_overlay_config0_u.uvh_rh10_gam_mmioh_overlay_config0_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_mmioh_overlay_config1_u","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_mmioh_overlay_config1_u.uvh_rh10_gam_mmioh_overlay_config1_s"],"text":"Each MMIO overlay pairs a raw word with identical common, YH and UV5 views ordered from low to high as reserved space then base then M_IO then N_IO then one undefined bit then enable."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_REDIRECT_CONFIG0","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_REDIRECT_CONFIG0_DEPTH","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_REDIRECT_CONFIG1","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_REDIRECT_CONFIG1_DEPTH","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_REDIRECT_CONFIG0_NASID_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_REDIRECT_CONFIG0_NASID_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_REDIRECT_CONFIG1_NASID_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_REDIRECT_CONFIG1_NASID_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_mmioh_redirect_config0_u","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_mmioh_redirect_config1_u"],"text":"On UV5 the two MMIO redirect tables start at 0x473800 and 0x474800 with 128 entries each, where every entry carries a 7-bit writable node address starting at bit 0 and reserves the remaining high bits, exposed through identical common, YH and UV5 views."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_PRESENT_0","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_PRESENT_TABLE","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_PRESENT_TABLE_DEPTH","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_RH10_GAM_GRU_OVERLAY_CONFIG","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_OVERLAY_CONFIG0_BASE_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_OVERLAY_CONFIG1_BASE_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_RH10_GAM_MMIOH_REDIRECT_CONFIG0_DEPTH","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_RH10_GAM_MMR_OVERLAY_CONFIG"],"text":"Register addresses and table depths shown here are revision-conditional and yield zero when the running UV generation is not listed, while generic base-shift helpers yield minus one off-revision, so callers must confirm the active generation before dereferencing the resulting address or depth."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_ipi_int_u.uvh_ipi_int_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_id_u.uvh_node_id_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_id_u.uvxh_node_id_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_present_0_u.uvh_node_present_0_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_addr_map_config_u.uvh_rh10_gam_addr_map_config_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_gru_overlay_config_u.uvh_rh10_gam_gru_overlay_config_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_mmioh_overlay_config0_u.uvh_rh10_gam_mmioh_overlay_config0_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_mmioh_redirect_config0_u.uvh_rh10_gam_mmioh_redirect_config0_s"],"text":"The fragments tag identity and telemetry portions as read-only, trigger and mapping controls such as node number, presence bitmaps, socket and key-width settings, overlay base and count fields, and redirect node addresses as read-write, and the IPI send control as a write-triggered action."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_id_u.uvxh_node_id_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_id_u.uvyh_node_id_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_node_id_u.uv4h_node_id_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_addr_map_config_u.uvh_rh10_gam_addr_map_config_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_gru_overlay_config_u.uvh_rh10_gam_gru_overlay_config_s","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::uvh_rh10_gam_mmioh_overlay_config0_u.uvh_rh10_gam_mmioh_overlay_config0_s"],"text":"Reserved and explicitly undefined spans separate functional fields in several registers and the upper node-identifier format changes width and meaning across families, so reusing one generation layout for another or assuming stability of non-functional bits can misdecode the register."}],"index_id":"99dbddb713e8d299bd55ae3ea6f9df9103f2fe09352557dba05a5a735dfe6c48","lane":79,"pass":1,"prefix_sha256":"90fbc6904033e42000ae762f7e22713ee62f438dcdedfc4bd7328bc76c81714c","prompt_sha256":"ee7b8783740f17eceb2a68b7cc578c6388620deebd1cd69f3923a7ad4ebccf8d","schema":"lx.extract.v1","sids_read":["arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_IPI_INT_VECTOR_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_ID","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_ID_FORCE1_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVXH_NODE_ID_NODE_ID_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_NODE_ID_NODE_ID_MASK","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV4H_NODE_ID_ROUTER_SELECT_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV3H_NODE_ID_ROUTER_SELECT_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_PRESENT_0","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVYH_NODE_PRESENT_0_NODES_SHFT","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UVH_NODE_PRESENT_1","arch/x86/include/asm/uv/uv_mmrs.h::UV